{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"agent_message","text":"The safe design is unconditional `yang.call` for every linked Python module: every module body can call a Python callable through `py/call-kw`, whose runtime dispatch consults `yang.call`, whether or not source contains a direct `yang.call/*` symbol. I’m also making the Python hook stage recognize `yang.call` as a runtime module (`py` and `pysp` are already treated that way); its dispatcher is not guest Python code and cannot carry the Python frontend’s site marks. The linker’s admission rule remains unchanged."}}
