{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_156","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-11-01 11:51:13 GMT  \nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-01 18:51:13 +07\n\n**Root cause and design choice.** In [lower.cljc:2097](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-py-fix/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2097), dependency detection only saw direct `yang.call/*` names. Python calls can reach `yang.call` indirectly through `py/call-kw`, so linked modules were missing a real dependency. I chose **(a): require `yang.call` unconditionally** for Python modules and SCC bundles; every module can use that call path. The manifest pins the dependency at [lower.cljc:2161](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-py-fix/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2161).\n\nThe `missing-site-set` refusal was a separate issue: the Python hook stage treated the shared `yang.call` dispatcher as guest Python code, though it has no Python site marks. [siteset.cljc:502](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-py-fix/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc:502) now passes that runtime module through; missing site sets for guest modules still refuse.\n\n**Slow-tier JVM results:**\n\n| Namespace | Result |\n|---|---:|\n| `yang.python.antlr.siteset-test` | 5 tests, 71 assertions, 0 failures/errors |\n| `yang.python.antlr.safepoint-test` | 19 tests, 144 assertions, 0 failures/errors |\n| `yin.vm.semantic.derive-test` | 1 test, 54 assertions, 0 failures/errors |\n| `yang.python.antlr.dht-import-test` | 1 test, 127 assertions, 0 failures/errors |\n| `yang.python.antlr.linked-prelude-test` | 8 tests, 82 assertions, 0 failures/errors |\n| `yang.python.antlr.linked-safepoint-test` | 10 tests, 53 assertions, 0 failures/errors |\n| `yang.python.antlr.e2e-test` | 42 tests, 714 assertions, 0 failures/errors |\n\nThe DHT artifact was regenerated to publish `yang.call` in its signed index. Its install counts and republish sequence now account for that runtime module. The linked prelude and safepoint manifest goldens were updated to their current S3-linked addresses. Both named e2e failures pass; no separate e2e defect remained.\n\n`bb test:sub:clj yang.python` passed: 28 namespaces, 265 tests, 0 failures. Kondo: 0 errors, 0 warnings. Cljstyle and `git diff --check` passed.\n\nCommitted as `6d6b7e71` (`fix(yang.python): link shared call runtime`) on `yangpython-link-reds`. Worktree is clean. Node/Dart verification remains with the orchestrator."}}
